<!--
    The Swift convention of functions the metadata did not bind (`option
    swiftinfer on|off`).

    Issue: the `swiftcall` arm binds `__swiftcall` only to functions Swift
    metadata places in a type. A closure's partial-apply forwarder keeps the C
    model, so the context it reads from swiftself (r13 / x20) is an
    uninitialised local (`long v2; // r13`), and a two-word Swift result is a
    128-bit integer split by `SUB168(v1,0)` / `SUB168(v1,8)`.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 prototype recovery. The decompile drive decodes the
    function and its direct callees (`p4_calls/kuna_swiftinfer.rs (seed)`); a
    body that reads swiftself on entry for anything but saving it decompiles
    under `__swiftcall` with the input named `swiftself`. The call-output type
    (`TypeOpCall::getOutputLocal`) of a two-word join whose words are read apart
    is `swift.pair`.

    The fixture `swift_infer_elf` is a stripped swiftc 6.3 build of
    `swift_infer_elf.swift` (recipe in the fixtures README): 0x24b0 is the
    partial-apply forwarder of `makeAdder`'s closure, 0x2840 is `usePair`, which
    reads both words `split` returns. Pass 1 (`option swiftinfer off`) is the
    BUG, pass 2 (the default) the FIX.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/swift_infer_elf</com>
  <com>option swiftmetadata on</com>
  <com>option swiftinfer off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x24b0</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2840</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/swift_infer_elf</com>
  <com>option swiftmetadata on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x24b0</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x2840</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="SWIFTINFER #1: off: the closure reads an uninitialised r13" min="1" max="1">int8 v2; // r13</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="SWIFTINFER #2: off: the pair is a 128-bit integer split apart" min="1" max="1">return SUB168\(v1,0\) - SUB168\(v1,8\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="SWIFTINFER #3: on: the closure takes its context as swiftself" min="1" max="1">int8 sub_24b0\(void \*swiftself\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="SWIFTINFER #4: on: the context is read through swiftself" min="1" max="1">return \(\(int8 \*\)swiftself\)\[2\] \+ 1;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="SWIFTINFER #5: on: the two-word result is a swift.pair" min="1" max="1">swift\.pair v1; // rdx:rax</stringmatch>
